// SkySynth on OMAR with per, model, check and setup (tutorial cache task, N=3 iterations: a smoke run, NOT 1:1 with SkySynth's Quick ~20).
// Run: omar run SkySynth.omar --input synth.ask="Build me a fast cache for the workload in workload.py. Ask me what you need to know before starting." --input synth.budget=3 --timeout-seconds 86400 --checkpoint-period tag --keep-workspaces
// Fix attempts of the delivery loop: the coder's `check` returns run_tests.py failures to the SAME conversation inside one invocation (SkySynth's
// TaskCompleted hook bounces to the same agent), so the coder is `per task`: fresh across iterations, continuous across fix attempts.
// Backends: Claude and Codex only. Models: Claude roles claude-sonnet-5-5 (SkySynth's tutorial recommends Sonnet for the loop, for
// cost); the lead claude-opus-5-5; the Codex coder runs Codex's default model. Every role but the lead is `per task`
// (SkySynth: "Run a fresh agent for each step"); the lead is one persistent Claude conversation.
// Hooks: each team gets `setup` = SkySynth's install.sh for its own backend, so the clone-reuse guard and the framework edit
// guard load for Claude and for Codex. The delivery hook (delivery_check.sh) is a `check` on the tasks that deliver.

team Kb(ctx : string)[kb_builder : Claude(model = "claude-sonnet-5-5") per task]
{
    setup "bash /home/you/skydiscover/skydiscover/synthesize/scripts/install.sh --agent claude ."
    input job : string
    output report : string

    task kb_builder(job) -> report within(1h)
    "$(ctx) Role: kb-builder (brief agents/1-specification/kb-builder.md), first build in ADAPT mode: adopt the reference systems already cloned in the run dir under specification/sources/ and specification/references/ instead of selecting sources; write at most 2 wiki pages into the knowledge base at $SKYDISCOVER_HOME; do not mine PRs or issues. A thin or failed build must not block anything: report what you managed. Then set report to a one-line summary. Context: $(job)"
}

team Coder(ctx : string)[coder : Codex per task]
{
    setup "bash /home/you/skydiscover/skydiscover/synthesize/scripts/install.sh --agent codex ."
    input boot_job : string
    input iter_job : string
    output booted : string
    output changed : string

    task coder(boot_job) -> booted within(2h)
    "$(ctx) Role: coding-agent, bootstrap mode (brief agents/2-synthesis-loop/coding-agent.md): build synthesis/evaluator/interface/ and synthesis/evaluator/benchmark/ (benchmark = workload.py replay on the tutorial cache, app_hit_rate, seeded) and an unscored first candidate in synthesis/impl/; it never becomes the trusted reference. Context: $(boot_job). Then set booted to a one-line summary."

    task coder(iter_job) -> changed within(3h)
    "$(ctx) Role: coding-agent, iteration mode: one change, fast tests, exit. Read plan.md ## Brief and ## Learnings (the critic feedback so far) and make the single change the brief asks for in synthesis/impl/. Your completion is checked by SkySynth's delivery hook (every kept test via run_tests.py --run): if it refuses, fix synthesis/impl/ so every kept test passes, change nothing else, and complete again. Previous feedback: $(iter_job). Then set changed to a one-line summary."
    check "bash /home/you/skysynth/delivery_check_wrap.sh tutorial"
}

team Synth(ctx : string)[
    lead : Claude(model = "claude-opus-5-5"),
    spec : Claude(model = "claude-sonnet-5-5") per task,
    planner : Claude(model = "claude-sonnet-5-5") per task,
    evaluator : Claude(model = "claude-sonnet-5-5") per task,
    auditor : Claude(model = "claude-sonnet-5-5") per task,
    critic : Claude(model = "claude-sonnet-5-5") per task
]
{
    setup "bash /home/you/skydiscover/skydiscover/synthesize/scripts/install.sh --agent claude ."
    input ask : string
    input budget : int
    output status : string
    output result : string

    action start : string
    action kbstatus : string
    action disc : string
    action settled : string
    action env : string
    action req : string
    action fixfail : string
    action fixed : string
    action go : string
    action hard : string
    action plan0 : string
    action refdone : string
    action iter_go : string
    action gated : string
    action scored : string
    action to_audit : string
    action to_critic : string
    action audited : string
    action feedback : string
    action phase3 : string
    action to_final_audit : string
    action to_report : string
    action final_audited : string
    action reported : string

    kb = Kb("SkySynth run by OMAR (tutorial cache task, 3 iterations: smoke, NOT a 1:1 run). Project dir: /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/project (contains workload.py). Run dir: /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache. This run dir is the one shared place for all roles: ignore any instruction to keep persistent files in your own worktree; every relative path in your brief (synthesis/..., specification/..., plan.md) means that run dir, never your current directory, and you must never create real synthesis/ or specification/ directories in your current directory: FIRST run `ln -sfn /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache/synthesis synthesis; ln -sfn /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache/specification specification; ln -sfn /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache/review review` there (the worker rules that tell you to keep files in your worktree are satisfied by these links, which resolve into the run dir), and write only the files the brief names, at their run-dir paths. Before every helper command run: export PYTHONPATH=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/framework SKYDISCOVER_RUNS=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs SKYDISCOVER_OUTPUTS=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/outputs SKYDISCOVER_HOME=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/home SKYDISCOVER_RUN=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1. The skydiscover framework you import and read is a READ-ONLY copy at /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/framework; skill dir: /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/framework/skydiscover/synthesize/workflow (read SKILL.md Rules That Hold Everywhere; your brief is agents/<phase>/<role>.md; layout in references/artifacts.md). Never modify the framework, any copy of it or the original checkout (a change fails the whole run). Never install packages or call external LLM APIs. Never kill or stop processes you did not start. Do exactly one role and mode as stated below, then set the output port named at the end to a one-line summary of what you did. Smoke limits: use at most 2 reference systems for discovery (small ones: one cache library or the tutorial workload, no deep PR mining), keep any subagent fan-out to 2, keep each test run under 30 s, and finish your role in as few steps as the brief allows.")
    coder = Coder("SkySynth run by OMAR (tutorial cache task, 3 iterations: smoke, NOT a 1:1 run). Project dir: /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/project (contains workload.py). Run dir: /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache. This run dir is the one shared place for all roles: ignore any instruction to keep persistent files in your own worktree; every relative path in your brief (synthesis/..., specification/..., plan.md) means that run dir, never your current directory, and you must never create real synthesis/ or specification/ directories in your current directory: FIRST run `ln -sfn /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache/synthesis synthesis; ln -sfn /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache/specification specification; ln -sfn /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache/review review` there (the worker rules that tell you to keep files in your worktree are satisfied by these links, which resolve into the run dir), and write only the files the brief names, at their run-dir paths. Before every helper command run: export PYTHONPATH=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/framework SKYDISCOVER_RUNS=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs SKYDISCOVER_OUTPUTS=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/outputs SKYDISCOVER_HOME=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/home SKYDISCOVER_RUN=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1. The skydiscover framework you import and read is a READ-ONLY copy at /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/framework; skill dir: /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/framework/skydiscover/synthesize/workflow (read SKILL.md Rules That Hold Everywhere; your brief is agents/<phase>/<role>.md; layout in references/artifacts.md). Never modify the framework, any copy of it or the original checkout (a change fails the whole run). Never install packages or call external LLM APIs. Never kill or stop processes you did not start. Do exactly one role and mode as stated below, then set the output port named at the end to a one-line summary of what you did. Smoke limits: use at most 2 reference systems for discovery (small ones: one cache library or the tutorial workload, no deep PR mining), keep any subagent fan-out to 2, keep each test run under 30 s, and finish your role in as few steps as the brief allows.")

    state have_ask : bool = false
    state have_budget : bool = false
    state ask_text : string = ""
    state n : int = 3
    state k : int = 0
    state check_retried : bool = false
    state req_seen : bool = false
    state kb_seen : bool = false
    state gate_done : bool = false

    reaction(ask, budget) -> start?, status? {=
        if let Some(a) = ask { self.ask_text = a.clone(); self.have_ask = true; }
        if let Some(b) = budget { self.n = b; self.have_budget = true; }
        if self.have_ask && self.have_budget {
            let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "setup"]).arg(&self.ask_text).output().unwrap();
            if !o.status.success() { panic!("setup failed: {}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
            start = Some(self.ask_text.clone());
            status = Some(format!("Phase 1: Initial Specification (budget {} iterations from run input)", self.n));
        }
    =}

    task lead(start) -> kbstatus within(1h)
    "$(ctx) Role: lead, Step 1 of SKILL.md Phase 1 (read it). The user ask is: $(start). Run spec.paths run tutorial-cache is already done (the run dir exists); write task.md in it with front matter domain: cache (and no checked_by key), read the knowledge base read-only, state and record the line knowledge base: cache, N tests, M findings, P wiki pages in the decision log, and do NOT run the spec-builder yourself. Then set kbstatus to a one-line summary."

    action kbstatus_ok : string
    reaction(kbstatus) -> kbstatus_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "lead-step1", "0"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after lead-step1 failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        kbstatus_ok = kbstatus.clone();
    =}

    task spec(kbstatus_ok) -> disc within(2h)
    "$(ctx) Role: spec-builder, mode discovery (brief agents/1-specification/spec-builder.md). Ground the cache domain in the reference systems. Context: $(kbstatus_ok). Then set disc to a one-line summary."

    action disc_ok : string
    reaction(disc) -> disc_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "spec-discovery", "0"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after spec-discovery failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        disc_ok = disc.clone();
    =}

    task lead(disc_ok) -> settled within(1h)
    "$(ctx) Role: lead, Step 2 of SKILL.md: settle every property question the sources or the task determine with decisions set ... --by ai --note, leave an optimization target out of the questions, then run decisions <run> answer so each still-open question gets its declared default (the operator is answering with defaults in this smoke run). Do not ask anyone anything. Discovery said: $(disc_ok). Then set settled to a one-line summary."

    action settled_ok : string
    reaction(settled) -> settled_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "lead-step2", "0"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after lead-step2 failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        settled_ok = settled.clone();
    =}

    task spec(settled_ok) -> env within(2h)
    "$(ctx) Role: spec-builder, mode environment (the score is a rate, so measure the resource limit and the ceiling for tutorial workload.py: FIFO baseline app_hit_rate is about 0.3886; the named workload is workload.py replay() so skip workload mode). Context: $(settled_ok). Then set env to a one-line summary."

    action env_ok : string
    reaction(env) -> env_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "spec-environment", "0"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after spec-environment failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        env_ok = env.clone();
    =}

    env_ok -> kb.job

    task spec(env_ok) -> req within(2h)
    "$(ctx) Role: spec-builder, mode requirements (the kb-builder is running in parallel with you and writes only under the knowledge base). Context: $(env_ok). Then set req to a one-line summary."

    action req_ok : string
    reaction(req) -> req_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "spec-requirements", "0"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after spec-requirements failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        req_ok = req.clone();
    =}

    reaction(req_ok, kb.report, fixed_ok) -> go?, fixfail?, status? {=
        if req_ok.is_some() { self.req_seen = true; }
        if let Some(r) = &report {
            let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "kb-builder", "0"]).output().unwrap();
            if !o.status.success() { panic!("after kb-builder failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
            let _ = r; self.kb_seen = true;
        }
        let ready = (self.req_seen && self.kb_seen) || fixed_ok.is_some();
        if ready && !self.gate_done {
            let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "check"]).output().unwrap();
            let text = format!("{}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr));
            if o.status.success() {
                self.gate_done = true;
                go = Some("run check exit 0".to_string());
                status = Some("Phase 1: run check passed, hardening next".to_string());
            } else if !self.check_retried {
                self.check_retried = true;
                fixfail = Some(text);
            } else {
                panic!("run check failed twice: {}", text);
            }
        }
    =}

    action fixed_ok : string
    task spec(fixfail) -> fixed within(1h)
    "$(ctx) Role: spec-builder, repair: run check failed with the output below; re-run the mode that owns each missing file (discovery for references, environment for the environment card) and nothing else. Output: $(fixfail). Then set fixed to a one-line summary."
    reaction(fixed) -> fixed_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "spec-repair", "0"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after spec-repair failed"); }
        fixed_ok = fixed.clone();
    =}

    task spec(go) -> hard within(1h)
    "$(ctx) Role: spec-builder, mode hardening (writes cards/properties.json). Context: $(go). Then set hard to a one-line summary."

    action hard_ok : string
    reaction(hard) -> hard_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "spec-hardening", "1"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after spec-hardening failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        hard_ok = hard.clone();
    =}

    task planner(hard_ok) -> plan0 within(1h)
    "$(ctx) Role: planner, seed mode (brief agents/2-synthesis-loop/planner.md): write synthesis/plan.md. Context: $(hard_ok). Then set plan0 to a one-line summary."

    action plan0_ok : string
    reaction(plan0) -> plan0_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "planner-seed", "1"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after planner-seed failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        plan0_ok = plan0.clone();
    =}

    plan0_ok -> coder.boot_job

    action boot_ok : string
    reaction(coder.booted) -> boot_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "coder-bootstrap", "1"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after coder-bootstrap failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        boot_ok = booted.clone();
    =}

    task evaluator(boot_ok) -> refdone within(2h)
    "$(ctx) Role: evaluator, mode correctness (brief agents/2-synthesis-loop/evaluator.md): write the trusted reference, mutants, and the kept tests with synthesis/tests/test.sh; every kept test passes validate_test.py. Keep the suite small (3 to 5 tests). Context: $(boot_ok). Then set refdone to a one-line summary."

    action refdone_ok : string
    reaction(refdone) -> refdone_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "evaluator-correctness", "1"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after evaluator-correctness failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        refdone_ok = refdone.clone();
    =}

    // One loop step: iteration 1 starts from refdone_ok; every later one from the critic's feedback. k counts finished iterations.
    reaction(refdone_ok, feedback_ok) -> iter_go?, phase3?, status? {=
        if refdone_ok.is_some() {
            iter_go = Some("iteration 1, no feedback yet".to_string());
            status = Some(format!("Phase 2: Synthesis Loop ({}/{} iterations)", self.k, self.n));
        } else {
            self.k += 1;
            status = Some(format!("Phase 2: Synthesis Loop ({}/{} iterations)", self.k, self.n));
            if self.k >= self.n { phase3 = Some("budget spent".to_string()); }
            else { iter_go = feedback_ok.clone(); }
        }
    =}
    iter_go -> coder.iter_job

    // SkySynth's delivery hook is the coder's `check`; this asserts it held (C-4) before the performance evaluator may score.
    reaction(coder.changed) -> gated, status? {=
        let a = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "coder-iteration", "1"]).output().unwrap();
        if !a.status.success() { panic!("after coder-iteration failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&a.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&a.stderr)); }
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "tests"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("delivery gate failed after the coder's check passed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        gated = Some("run_tests.py exit 0".to_string());
        status = Some(format!("Phase 2: Synthesis Loop ({}/{} iterations), tests pass, measuring", self.k, self.n));
    =}

    task evaluator(gated) -> scored within(2h)
    "$(ctx) Role: evaluator, mode performance (brief agents/2-synthesis-loop/evaluator.md): measure at the scored configuration, append the leaderboard row (and the FIFO baseline row), take a held-out draw with seed=123 before --became-best, write the checkpoint with spec.checkpoint snapshot right after the leaderboard append. Context: $(gated). Then set scored to a one-line summary."

    // Measured, then the mechanical audit decision (SKILL.md: new best, or first candidate to beat the baseline).
    reaction(scored) -> to_audit?, to_critic?, status? {=
        let a = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "evaluator-performance", "1"]).output().unwrap();
        if !a.status.success() { panic!("after evaluator-performance failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&a.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&a.stderr)); }
        let lb = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "lb"]).output().unwrap();
        let m = String::from_utf8_lossy(&lb.stdout).trim().to_string();
        let d = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "auditdec"]).output().unwrap();
        let dec = String::from_utf8_lossy(&d.stdout).trim().to_string();
        let line = format!("{}; audit decision: {}", m, dec);
        status = Some(format!("Phase 2: Synthesis Loop ({}/{} iterations), measured: {}", self.k, self.n, line));
        if dec.starts_with("run") { to_audit = Some(line); } else { to_critic = Some(line); }
    =}

    task auditor(to_audit) -> audited within(2h)
    "$(ctx) Role: auditor (brief agents/2-synthesis-loop/auditor.md), per-iteration pass (mechanical audit decision said run): audit the candidate in synthesis/impl/ against the kept tests and the spec for reward hacks (smoke: one round, at most 2 probes), add any confirmed finding through the findings CLI, and stamp with spec.checkpoint stamp-audit. Measured state and decision: $(to_audit). Then set audited to a one-line summary."

    action audited_ok : string
    reaction(audited) -> audited_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "auditor-iteration", "1"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after auditor-iteration failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        audited_ok = audited.clone();
    =}

    task critic(to_critic, audited_ok) -> feedback within(45min)
    "$(ctx) Role: critic (brief agents/2-synthesis-loop/critic.md). Read the leaderboard and plan.md, write ranked file:line feedback, append this iteration to plan.md ## Learnings only. Do not edit code. The Learnings append is the only file you write. Measured state: $(to_critic) $(audited_ok). Then set feedback to a one-line summary."

    action feedback_ok : string
    reaction(feedback) -> feedback_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "critic", "1"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after critic failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        feedback_ok = feedback.clone();
    =}

    // Final audit stamp: audit only if the existing stamp does not cover the delivered candidate (audit_covers), as run finish requires.
    reaction(phase3) -> to_final_audit?, to_report?, status? {=
        let c = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "auditcov"]).output().unwrap();
        let t = String::from_utf8_lossy(&c.stdout).trim().to_string();
        status = Some(format!("Phase 3: Final Deliverables ({} of {} iterations), final audit stamp: {}", self.k, self.n, t));
        if t.starts_with("covered") { to_report = Some(t); } else { to_final_audit = Some(t); }
    =}

    task auditor(to_final_audit) -> final_audited within(2h)
    "$(ctx) Role: auditor (brief agents/2-synthesis-loop/auditor.md), mode completeness/coverage on the delivered candidate (smoke: one round, at most 2 probes): add any confirmed finding through the findings CLI and ALWAYS write the stamp with spec.checkpoint stamp-audit so run finish can proceed. Stamp state: $(to_final_audit). Then set final_audited to a one-line summary."

    action final_audited_ok : string
    reaction(final_audited) -> final_audited_ok {=
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "auditor-final", "1"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("after auditor-final failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        final_audited_ok = final_audited.clone();
    =}

    task lead(to_report, final_audited_ok) -> reported within(1h)
    "$(ctx) Role: lead, final step: write report.md in the run dir (the lead writes it). It must contain the text k of N iterations, the reason the loop ended, the best score against the 0.3886 FIFO baseline, and say this is a scoped smoke run (production-ready not claimed; the security/reliability/attack lenses and the proof path were not run; audit decisions are in /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/audit-decisions.log). Context: $(to_report) $(final_audited_ok). Then set reported to a one-line summary."
    check "bash /home/you/skysynth/delivery_check_wrap.sh tutorial"

    reaction(reported) -> result?, status? {=
        let a = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "after", "lead-final", "1"]).output().unwrap();
        if !a.status.success() { panic!("after lead-final failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&a.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&a.stderr)); }
        let o = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "finish"]).output().unwrap();
        if !o.status.success() { panic!("run finish failed: {}{}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout), String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stderr)); }
        let r = std::process::Command::new("/home/you/skysynth/helper.sh").args(["tutorial", "recheck"]).output().unwrap();
        if !r.status.success() { panic!("final re-check failed: {}", String::from_utf8_lossy(&r.stderr)); }
        result = Some(String::from_utf8_lossy(&o.stdout).trim().to_string());
        status = Some(format!("Phase 3: Final Deliverables ({} of {} iterations)", self.k, self.n));
        request_stop();
    =}
}

main SkySynth {
    synth = Synth("SkySynth run by OMAR (tutorial cache task, 3 iterations: smoke, NOT a 1:1 run). Project dir: /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/project (contains workload.py). Run dir: /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache. This run dir is the one shared place for all roles: ignore any instruction to keep persistent files in your own worktree; every relative path in your brief (synthesis/..., specification/..., plan.md) means that run dir, never your current directory, and you must never create real synthesis/ or specification/ directories in your current directory: FIRST run `ln -sfn /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache/synthesis synthesis; ln -sfn /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache/specification specification; ln -sfn /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache/review review` there (the worker rules that tell you to keep files in your worktree are satisfied by these links, which resolve into the run dir), and write only the files the brief names, at their run-dir paths. Before every helper command run: export PYTHONPATH=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/framework SKYDISCOVER_RUNS=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs SKYDISCOVER_OUTPUTS=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/outputs SKYDISCOVER_HOME=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/home SKYDISCOVER_RUN=/home/you/skysynth/tutorial/runs/tutorial-cache PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1. The skydiscover framework you import and read is a READ-ONLY copy at /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/framework; skill dir: /home/you/skysynth/tutorial/framework/skydiscover/synthesize/workflow (read SKILL.md Rules That Hold Everywhere; your brief is agents/<phase>/<role>.md; layout in references/artifacts.md). Never modify the framework, any copy of it or the original checkout (a change fails the whole run). Never install packages or call external LLM APIs. Never kill or stop processes you did not start. Do exactly one role and mode as stated below, then set the output port named at the end to a one-line summary of what you did. Smoke limits: use at most 2 reference systems for discovery (small ones: one cache library or the tutorial workload, no deep PR mining), keep any subagent fan-out to 2, keep each test run under 30 s, and finish your role in as few steps as the brief allows.")
}
